<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kulottunga III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1178–1218</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Kulottunga Chola III</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kulottunga III was the last strong king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola Empire</a>, reigning from 1178 to 1218. He campaigned successfully against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandyas</a>, sacking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madurai">Madurai</a>, and against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysalas</a> and the Sinhalese, and built the Kampaharesvara temple at Thirubuvanam. After his reign Chola power declined rapidly before the rising Pandyas and Hoysalas.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kulottunga-iii.jpg" alt="Kulottunga III" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arulghsr · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kulothunga_Chola_III_statchu_in_penneswaraar_temple,_peneswara_madam_villege_krishnagiri_district.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
